    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Notes\n\n1) **Combustion of Fuel Gases**: Combustion of a fuel gas creates a flue gas with higher density than the fuel gas and the combustion air. This is due to stoichiometric combustion reactions.\n\n2) **Volume at Standard Pressure**: All volume measurements are at standard pressure conditions.\n\n## Categories\n\n### Solids\nIncludes coal types (Anthracite, Bituminous, Lignite), coke, charcoal, peat, and wood.\n\n### Gases\nIncludes hydrocarbon gases such as Butane, Propane, and Natural Gas.\n\n### Fluids\nIncludes liquid fuels such as Gas Oil and Heavy Fuel Oil.\n\n## Unit Systems\n\n- **Metric**: m³/kg for solids, m³/m³ for gases, m³/liter for fluids\n- **Imperial**: ft³/lb for solids, ft³/ft³ for gases, ft³/gallon for fluids"
